dtinfo and the DocBook tools optional, with their LMDB and Tcl checks.

configure stops without liblmdb and without Tcl's tclConfig.sh, but only two
parts of CDE use them: dtinfo, the information-library browser (LMDB, through
DtMmdb), and programs/dtdocbook, the DocBook tools (LMDB, and Tcl in
instant). Amix has neither library: LMDB 0.9 needs process-shared POSIX
mutexes or POSIX semaphores, and nothing on the box needs Tcl. So:
- configure.ac: --disable-dtinfo and --disable-dtdocbook (both default to
  enabled, as before); liblmdb is checked only when either is built, Tcl
  only when dtdocbook is; BUILD_MMDB when either is;
- lib/Makefile.am: DtMmdb, the database library only those two use, joins
  SUBDIRS only with BUILD_MMDB;
- programs/Makefile.am: dtinfo and dtdocbook join SUBDIRS only when built;
- the C locale's app-defaults (Dtinfo), message catalogues (dtinfo,
  dtinfo_start) and action types (dtinfo.dt), and the ToolTalk types
  (dtinfo, dtinfo_start), are made only when dtinfo is.
With both enabled nothing changes. dtdocbook2man and dtdocbook2sdl are
still configured, so a build can run them through tools built for the
build host to make the manual pages and help volumes.

--- a/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -234,6 +234,18 @@
 )
 AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DOCS], [test -z "$disable_docs"])
 
+dnl dtinfo (needs liblmdb) and the DocBook tools in programs/dtdocbook (need
+dnl liblmdb and Tcl) are optional; their libraries are checked only for them
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([dtinfo],
+        AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-dtinfo], [Do not build dtinfo (default=no)]),
+        [], [enable_dtinfo=yes])
+AC_ARG_ENABLE([dtdocbook],
+        AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-dtdocbook], [Do not build the DocBook tools (default=no)]),
+        [], [enable_dtdocbook=yes])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTINFO], [test "x$enable_dtinfo" = xyes])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_DTDOCBOOK], [test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([BUILD_MMDB], [test "x$enable_dtinfo" = xyes || test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes])
+
 dnl Xrender usage
 AC_ARG_ENABLE([xrender],
         AS_HELP_STRING([--disable-xrender], [Disable use of the Xrender extension (default=auto)]),
@@ -499,10 +511,13 @@
              [${EXTRA_INCS} ${EXTRA_LIBS}])
 AC_SUBST(JPEGLIB)
 
-dnl lmdb
+dnl lmdb, for dtinfo and the DocBook tools only
+LMDBLIB=""
+if test "x$enable_dtinfo" = xyes || test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes; then
 AC_CHECK_LIB(lmdb, mdb_version, [LMDBLIB="-llmdb"],
              [AC_MSG_ERROR([liblmdb not found, please install it])],
              [${EXTRA_INCS} ${EXTRA_LIBS}])
+fi
 AC_SUBST(LMDBLIB)
 
 dnl Setup XTOOLLIB - we do it in this specific order to avoid ordering
@@ -564,10 +579,12 @@
 
 AM_CONDITIONAL([HAS_UTEMPTER_LIBRARY], [test "x$ac_cv_lib_utempter_utempter_add_record" = "xyes"])
 
-dnl Figure out TCL
-
+dnl Figure out TCL, for the DocBook tools only
+
+AS_IF([test "x$enable_dtdocbook" = xyes], [
 SC_PATH_TCLCONFIG
 SC_LOAD_TCLCONFIG
+])
 
